From d1387c4ab55d88f42dde4c7ab89481573992e215 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eddy Sangalli <eddyrodrigues@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:11:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(frontend): multistream, preset as a document, exit
 question

Multistream (widgets/FreeMixMultistream.cpp): up to four streaming
destinations besides the main one. Each is an output of its own that reuses
the video and audio encoders of the main stream; they go on air with it and
stop with it, and a destination switched on while live starts at once. The
list is kept per profile in freemix-destinos.json and is edited through the
control server, vendor "freemix" (get_destinations, set_destinations, event
destinations_changed). RTMP/RTMPS, SRT and RIST addresses.

Preset as a document (widgets/FreeMixPreset.cpp): a copy of the scene
collection as it was when opened, or last saved on purpose, is kept next to
it ("<name>.json.salvo"). Vendor requests save_preset and get_preset.

Exit question: "save the changes to the current preset?" with Save and
close / Discard changes and close / Cancel, as in the reference program;
discarding restores the kept copy after the final save. Recording or
streaming adds a warning above the question. Texts are FreeMix.Close.* in
the language files.

Smaller fixes: the Output title is refreshed after a preset change; the
centre mark of the safe-area guides has arms of equal length.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
